      "question": "Who can treat an injured street dog in Port Blair?",
      "response": "An injured street dog needs prompt treatment by a veterinarian; a trained animal-rescue service may help with safe transport.\n\nKeep people and animals back, approach only if safe, and minimise handling. If there is heavy bleeding, breathing trouble, collapse, or major trauma, arrange urgent veterinary transport without offering food or water.\n\nThese institutions are listed in the sources, but clinical treatment access remains unconfirmed:\n\n- Veterinary Hospital, Junglighat — Junglighat — institution listed; clinical treatment access is unconfirmed. Clinical contact: 03192-232252.\n\nA treatment listing alone does not establish rescue pickup or current availability. Call before travelling to confirm treatment and admission for this animal and the correct emergency location.",
